*.sln
build
.git-gitlab

Radiant/Shaders/SPIRV/Bin/

# ImGui saves the editor layout next to the working dir; it is per-user state
Editor/imgui.ini
imgui.ini

# Fetched by scripts/MacOS/Setup.sh (not submodules)
ThirdParty/optick/
ThirdParty/volk/

# Generated by scripts/GenVersion.sh
Desert/Common/Source/Common/Core/Version.gen.hpp

# Cooked artifacts (mesh/texture cooks, SPIR-V shader cache) — machine-local, content-addressed
Cooked/

# ...with one deliberate exception. A texture only becomes referenceable by a .demat once a .tex exists
# under Cooked/Textures/ carrying its handle, and the drag-drop importer mints that handle from the
# texture's ABSOLUTE path — so a texture the repo itself ships would get a different handle on every
# machine and every material pointing at it would resolve to nothing. This one .tex is therefore SOURCE,
# not a cook: its handle is fixed and its SourcePath is relative. The importer preserves the handle of an
# existing .tex, so re-cooking it changes nothing.
#
# Re-included one directory level at a time, and the intermediate `/*` lines are load-bearing: git will
# not look inside a directory it has already excluded, so `!.../T_Checker.tex` alone matches nothing.
# Each level is re-ignored immediately after being opened, which is what keeps the other ~660 cooked
# files (shader cache, pipeline cache, mesh cooks) ignored.
!Editor/Cooked/
Editor/Cooked/*
!Editor/Cooked/Textures/
Editor/Cooked/Textures/*
!Editor/Cooked/Textures/T_Checker.tex

# Fetched by scripts/MacOS/Setup.sh (not a submodule)
ThirdParty/meshoptimizer/
dist/

# Optional: cloned by the user to enable dlib face tracking (see BuildScripts/ThirdParty/Dlib.lua)
ThirdParty/dlib/

# Premake-generated build files (source of truth = premake5.lua; regenerate via
# scripts/MacOS/Setup.sh / BuildMacOS.sh)
*.make
Makefile

# Runtime logs
*.log
engine_log.txt

# Editor autosaves. Machine-written copies of a scene: tracking them means every schema change drags
# extra files behind it, and a stale autosave left on an old schema is a file in the repository that
# keeps the old format alive.
Editor/Resources/Assets/Scenes/Autosave/

# macOS Finder junk
.DS_Store

# --- Cloud programme reference material -------------------------------------------------------------
# The two SIGGRAPH PDFs (63 MB) are third-party conference material. Our analysis of them is committed
# (Docs/Clouds/*.md); the papers themselves are not ours to redistribute.
Docs/Clouds/*.pdf

# Material copied out of the Unreal editor: the material-graph dump and screenshots of Epic's UI. The
# waiver on file (Docs/Clouds/LICENCE_RECORD.md) covers USING it; committing Epic's asset verbatim into
# this repository is a different question and is not one to answer by accident. Our own extracted
# analysis lives in Docs/Clouds/UEReference/Documentation/ and IS committed.
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/*.png
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/*.graph.txt
# Epic's own source, dropped here to be cited line by line. Local only: the licence record covers using
# it as a reference, not redistributing it in our tree. Keep UE's own layout underneath
# (Engine/Shaders/Private/...) so a citation stays checkable, and record the engine version beside it —
# line numbers mean nothing against an unnamed release.
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/Source/

# Scratch git worktrees created by tooling. They are checkouts, not content.
.claude/worktrees/

# Gauntlet runs: the LEDGER is the point and is committed -- STATE.md, BAR.md, RUBRIC.md,
# every verdict and every reveal receipt. The paired images are not: they are copies of
# frames that already exist elsewhere, 40 tiles a sweep, and Docs/Clouds/Shots is already
# 508 MB of a 1.6 GB repository that has blown a CI checkout timeout once (see task D4).
.gauntlet/*/rounds/*/ab/
